<title>SOUTH AFRICA: DMG to advise on S.African airports sale.</title>
<headline>DMG to advise on S.African airports sale.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African government said on Monday it had appointed Deutsche Morgan Grenfell (DMG) to advise on the restructuring and part privatisation of the state-owned Airports Company.  </p>
<p>The intention is to sell up to 49 percent of the concern, which operates South Africa's major airports.  </p>
<p>Three groups were shortlisted for the role of adviser: SBC Warburg in partnership with Gobodo Inc, a firm of accountants and consultants; Standard Corporate and Merchant Bank in partnership with Morgan Stanley and Coordinated Management Consulting; and DMG.</p>
<p>Several foreign firms have expressed interest in taking a stake in the company.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
